{"text": ". \u2018 . ATTACHMENT D\n\nDear TAN Volunteer:\n\nThe Connecticut General Assembly is nearing a vote on\nbill (s) that would require (most, all) employers\nto separate their smoking and nonsmoking employees.\n\nWe oppose this (these) bill(s) for the following reasons:\n\n\u00a9 Public smoking legislation will result in higher\ncosts for the already overburdened and inflation-\nridden businesses here in Connecticut.\n\no The business establishments in our state have enough\nto worry about without adding another unnecessary\nregulation to the law books.\n\n\u00a9 Respect, tolerance and acconmodation are and must re-\nmain th\u00e9 business of people, not governments.\n\n\u00a9 Law enforcenent officers don't have the time to spend\nchasing smokers. They don't, that is, if society still\nwants Tapists, murderers and muggers pursued.\n\nIf you agree with our position, please contact your state\nrepresentative and senator at the address below:\n\nState Capital Building\n210 Capital Avenue\nHartford, CT 06106\n\nI have enclosed a list of the menbers of the General Assembly\nfor your information.\n\nIf you write, it would b\u00e9 most helpful if you would send me a\ncopy of your letter and any response you receive.\n\nWith your help, we can win the battle against this costly and\ndiscriminatory legislation.\n\nSincerely,\n\n069625089\n\n680579640\nPRODUCED FROM B&W WEB SITE",
